  "answer": "",
  "mistakes": [],
  "hints": [
    "a ≡ 1 (mod 5) means 5 | (a − 1), so a = 5k + 1 for some integer k.",
    "Show a² = 5·(integer) + 1."
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Since $5 \\mid (a - 1)$, $a = 5k + 1$ for some integer $k$.",
    "$a^2 = 25k^2 + 10k + 1 = 5(5k^2 + 2k) + 1$, so $5 \\mid (a^2 - 1)$, that is, $a^2 \\equiv 1 \\pmod 5$. $\\blacksquare$"
  ],
